## RF caveat

Random Forest is fundamentally a hard classifier; its per-class
probabilities are not calibrated as proportions of admixture.
Low CCC against RF is expected and not by itself a defect of
popout. The **hard-call confusion matrix** is the meaningful
comparison against RF; the soft-proportion comparisons against
FLARE and Rye are the calibrated ones.
